n the view for app builds before 0.1.93. Admin (`require_admin`): `GET /api/v1/admin/icp-requests` (the queue: every customer's open and sent requests, the sent ones first, oldest first, with `customer_name`), `GET|POST /api/v1/admin/customers/{id}/icp-requests` (POST `user_id`: one open request per person, so asking again turns theirs into SimpL's and re-sends the link; both lists carry `missing`, `answers` as label/text lines and `built` (filters, signals, prompts on its ICP)), `PATCH /api/v1/admin/icp-requests/{id}` (`status: done | cancelled`, `icp_id` of the same customer), `POST /api/v1/admin/icp-requests/{id}/activate`, `DELETE /api/v1/admin/icp-requests/{id}` (for good: the row, and its ICP in review with the ICP delete's cascade unless that ICP is on; an ICP it was only linked to stays; 409 while its price offer waits for a signature or is signed and not applied). Sending creates the ICP switched off, in review (`sales.icp` with the request's id, like the onboarding's session id; `icp_request.icp_id` set): it is listed with the customer's ICPs with minimum company score 0, SimpL builds it in the customer's chat (`open_icp_config_workspace` on it hands the agent the request's answers, `icp_request.review_brief`, and says it is in review and switched off), and switching it on any other way is refused (409) while the request is open. Its price (pay-per-call customers, migration 20261012191500_icp_request_price, `services/icp_request_price.py`): `POST .../{id}/price-estimate` counts the companies the saved filters match (the page calls it on leaving Companies; same pool calculator and tiers as the onboarding's estimate, `price_estimate` on the request); submit waits for it up to 25 s and, when it differs from what the customer's new ICPs cost today (the adopted order's future price, else EUR 70) and the customer signed the current terms, prepares an offer (`sales.legal_agreement`, context migration, order kind `pay_per_call_new_icp`: every other ICP at its price in force plus the new one) that the owner or billing admin signs at the end of the page (others see it in the pending-agreement prompt); `POST .../{id}/offer` prepares it again. No offer is prepared while another of the customer's offers is in flight (waiting for its signature, or signed and not applied yet; the newest offer is the one in force): the send still works, and `POST /api/v1/admin/icp-requests/{id}/offer` sends it once the other is done (409 with the reason meanwhile). ICPs still in review are left out of other offers' orders. Views carry `price`, `card` (Stripe default card, brand and last 4) and `needs_card`. Activate refuses a pay-per-call customer with no card (strict Stripe read) or an offer not signed, then switches the ICP on, assigns it to the person and to everyone who sends (not a billing manager) already in from the page's invites, sets the signed price as the ICP's override and records the offer as applied (inside its execution lease, like a move), sets a minimum company score above 1 back to 0 (review ICPs were created with 3 until 2026-10-15), closes the request as done and emails the person that it is live (`icp_request_email.notify_live`, reply-to the admin; best effort); with nothing to sign the price job gives it today's new-ICP price. Two offers signed for two requests at once: only the latest signed one can be applied, the other is prepared again. The link email (`/icp/new?request=<id>`, reply-to the admin) is sent by the customer access job once the person can open the app (account on, person on, billing open), up to 3 tries. `sales.customer_answers` (migration 20261012154200_customer_answers) holds each customer's Voice and Sources in the form's shape (`training_materials`), filled once by `scripts/convert_customer_answers.py` (dry run by default, `--apply` stores): one DeepSeek turn per customer reads the customer-level voice guide, value props and company brief (else the latest ICP's), and what the customer wrote at onboarding wins field by field; booking links are dropped.
