stomer set up (ICPs, voice, team, accounts) stays. A move that bills per call (`plan: pay_per_call`, or `keep` for a customer already on it) runs only with the customer's accepted agreement for the same `switch_id` and the exact same request (see Legal agreements below), else 409 before anything is written; `growth`, `none` and `keep` on a seat plan need none. Bringing back an `also_customer_ids` organization that is not already on pay per call with a pay-per-call plan is refused (409): it needs its own agreement. `PUT /api/v1/admin/customers/{id}/ui-version` (`ui_version: classic | v2`, `user_ids?`) moves people between the classic app and the new Home. Each person also turns the new Home on and off from their profile in simpl_sales (NULL = never chose: the classic app with an invitation to try it; `classic`; `v2`); everyone already signed up was set to NULL by migration 20261008d_user_ui_version_opt_in. A person added to a company without a Home of their own lands on the new Home when the company has no active people yet (a new customer), otherwise on the one most of their active teammates have (trigger, migrations 20261005_user_ui_version_follows_team and 20261006_user_ui_version_everyone). Logic in `services/pay_per_call_move.py`.
