- ROI vendor quiz (token, not JWT; the person's survey token): `src/simpl_api/api/v1/roi_vendor_quiz.py`, service `services/roi_vendor_quiz.py`, page `/roi/fornitori/<token>` in simpl_dashboard.
  - `GET /roi/vendors/quiz?token=` lists the vendors whose `reviewer` is that person, largest spend first, with spend, payers, samples, the proposal and the current answer. It also returns the live catalog (COGS included), the roster and, for Luca only, the trips. A vendor whose every line sits in a trip (`roi.trip_lines` with a `trip_id`; a released line counts as outside) is left out here and in the admin progress; it comes back once one of its lines is outside any trip.
  - `POST .../answer` writes a vendor assignment valid from the start, with `covers_months` (default 1) when each payment covers several months. It refuses a vendor that is not the person's, an unknown mode, a dead initiative, a person not on the roster or a spread on a mode that cannot spread.
  - `POST .../accept` confirms the proposals of the listed vendors that have no answer yet; it never overwrites an answer.
  - `POST .../pass` hands a vendor along the chain Raffaele, then Nicolò, then Luca.
